  "body": "## Result\n\nProves the exact rank-one paid-call tariff for a bipartite family of central commutators in the class-two group `H(m,n)`. For any finite bipartite edge set and edge multiplicities `p_ij`, the target with `p_ij` distinct dirty roles carrying `z_ij = x_i y_j x_i y_j` has minimum exactly `4 * sum(p_ij)` in the full formal `F2[H(m,n)]` model, for every finite dirty-register count. The edgewise four-call construction attains the bound. The first cyclic case is `K2,2`: four distinct central outputs, exact cost 16.\n\nThe lower bound uses one `UT3(F2)` quotient and its contragredient per active edge. Each label's column and row frames must span the disjoint sum of its incident target spaces; rank-nullity then sums to `4 * sum(p_ij)`. This extends the shared-middle path tariff to arbitrary bipartite incidence patterns, including a cycle. It does not claim a supplier implementation, selected-moment improvement, or new kappa.\n\n## Evidence and replay\n\nThe stdlib-only exact verifier checks the 256-element `H(2,2)` group law, every quotient and dual homomorphism on all group pairs, the 16-call `K2,2` word in the full formal algebra, a weighted six-target word, all 16 one-call omissions, a wrong-label control, and dirty spectators. The proof, package metadata/source pins, direct replay, and whitespace check pass locally under Python 3.14.7. Python 3.12 is unavailable locally; the registered Python 3.12 replay is left to CI. No hosted CI result is claimed.\n\nReproduce with:\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/heisenberg-commutator-incidence-seedb054 --check-only\npython3 -I -B research/heisenberg-commutator-incidence-seedb054/verify.py\n```\n\n## Pins and attribution\n\n- Base/main: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`\n- Task seed: `b054c63f8969592c7c1608ddeee294e9`; `bit-mechanisms`, priority revision 4\n- Selected-record SHA-256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`\n- Claim and correction: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1167#discussioncomment-18938788 and #18938817\n- Predecessors: merged UT4 shared-middle tariff; open PR #2175 (UT4 z/uz), #1816 (two central UT4 targets), and #2103 (UT5 four-role mixed-root target). These have different group/target incidence.\n\nThe pinned baseline returns `PASS_RESEARCH_BASELINE_BINDINGS_ONLY` and identifies the complex supplier as binding; this package does not affect that supplier or the selected bound. Prepared with substantial OpenAI Codex GPT-6 assistance in scope selection, derivation, implementation, verification and writing. No independent human review or proof-kernel verification is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n",
